{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BLOCKED on frowsy-beggarly-mammoth's gate fix. Gerrit change 1615 (patch set 2) is complete and carries LLM-Review +1, but cannot obtain Verified +1 for a reason unrelated to this work.\n\nRoot cause, reproduced: .github/mutation-shards.toml lists .github/workflows/test.yml in global_support, and scripts/mutation_gate.py::select_shards returns tuple(manifest.shards) - every shard - when ANY changed path matches a global_support pattern, overriding the all-shards:false workflow input. This ticket must edit test.yml (AC6: the pytest -m external lane is one of the six unguarded lanes in scope), so the change selects all 7 shards (signing, reducer-processors, next-batch, gates, validate, compact-policy, push-policy) = 14 base+head mutation passes inside _mutation.yml's timeout-minutes: 30. Verified locally against this diff: 'SELECTED: all 7 => all shards selected? True'.\n\nIt is a timeout, not a flake or a race: two independent runs cancelled at the same mark - run 31560638673 at 30m16s (03:39:25->04:09:41) and run 31562494026 at 30m17s (04:16:23->04:46:40). GitHub reports a timed-out job as 'cancelled', which the CI bot converts to Verified -1. recheck therefore cannot clear it; I stopped rechecking after proving this.\n\nEverything else is green on both runs: all four pytest cells passed (no s3_doctor flake on the second), and no --timeout fired anywhere, so the per-test budgets added by this ticket are not implicated in any failure.\n\nResolution path (operator decision): a dedicated agent is implementing frowsy-beggarly-mammoth as (1) drop .github/workflows/test.yml from global_support and (2) a measured raise of the mutation job's timeout-minutes in the SAME change - the second part is what lets the fix pass its own gate, since mutation-shards.toml is itself in global_support and would otherwise self-block. No admin bypass.\n\nNext action on this ticket: once that fix merges to origin/main, rebase 1615 onto fresh origin/main (keeping the Change-Id), re-push, collect both votes, submit, then verify ACs and close. No code change is expected here - the work itself is done and reviewed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786510948282783001,"uuid":"d2b72d3a-b1b1-4082-93a6-99fa79c03628"}